/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/identity-classes.mem:60:''SEATED ⊥ RAISED keeps the class law intact through the passage.'' The Herm's zero persona-slot ceiling bars a ''SEATED'' persona root — a human's key RESTING on a crossroads. It bars nothing about a ''RAISED'' cap: those arrive WITH a recognised operator, ride that operator's own keys, and stop standing when the recognition stops. The at-rest state never changes, so a stolen disk still yields nothing of anybody's person, and a herm may grow a house without ever becoming a place that keeps one. <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor">>
