/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/spirit-handback-field-collision-ii.mem:99:''ANTI-PATTERN.'' ''Willow's prefix-pruning + hostile-clock'': a newer short-path entry silently tombstones a whole subtree, and a skewed/hostile clock weaponizes "newer" (https://willowprotocol.org/specs/data-model/). This is a live, measured instance of exactly why `epoch-binding-surfaces.mem` KILLED the rolling-window shape ("a set answers ''is this listed'', never ''is this newer''") and why we hold "correct even if all timestamps were zero." Do not let any migration marker resolve on a self-asserted time.
