/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody.mem:218:# ''Preflight, before any write.'' The vessel reads every target row and every relation, the names rows and the handle-book among them: a row that stands and does not read whole refuses here, by its own name. The check of the board reads and never writes: a board this vessel never held reads as holding no event. A founded place stands here, the hearth the restored face binds stands (its seed charter, or the hearth an admit joined it to), and a face above index zero rides beside a lit founding face. The root's public key derives from its seed, the roster line names that key, and the prefix and signer name match what the root itself derives. The carried key history verifies whole, from the inception that root derives. ''The face's CURRENT key history still accepts the root'': every key event this vessel reads for the face, off the carried log and off its own board, folds through the one reader of key histories, and the newest event of that lineage still names this root as the operating key and still commits recovery to this root's own recovery key, or reads as the typed first enrolment this root signed. A rotation still open to contest counts as the newest event. A history that forks refuses: no reader settles a fork by order. An event that fails its own proof moves nothing, so nobody blocks a restore by planting one. No root of this face stands here. The target handle-index holds no other root, no other roster line and no lit face; an orphan root row there matches the bundle's key. No `face-proof-key` row stands there under other bytes.
