/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/swarm-harvest/the-crux-first-secret-sharing-vs-independent-d6ddd5.mem:391:**The generalization: nobody does threshold *signing*.** Every archive is signed by one online key. Where m-of-n appears it is in one of two adjacent places — **recovering** a lost secret (Debian 3-of-5) or **admitting** a key to the trust set (Debian 2 DDs, kernel.org 2 account holders, Arch 3 master keys). And every recovery in the record has the same shape: *mint a new key, get humans to sign it out of band, re-sign or re-point the archive, and push the new anchor through the old key if it still works — by hand if it doesn't.*
