/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/wiki-layer-ontology.mem:186:''Three outcomes, and only two of them decide anything.'' A rule may ROUTE a title, a rule may WITHHOLD it, or no rule may reach it at all — and the third names a ''router gap'', a fault in the cascade rather than a property of the tiddler. Read as one outcome, a gap drops the write in silence: the save resolves, the surface shows the edit, nothing persists, and the work vanishes at the next boot with nothing anywhere to read. So a gap MUST announce itself and MUST still land the write at the write layer.
