/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths.mem:273:# ''The three-plane negentropy crossing — Codex Luna internet swarm to Claude/Lares crew, 2026-09-26.'' Current prior art converges around one useful reading: local-first replicas/CRDTs govern causal data convergence; content addressing, SRI, reproducible builds, and SLSA govern bytes/build provenance; capability security, DID verification relationships, and explicit audience binding govern relation authority; relays, Compose, Caddy/NGINX, and NAT aids govern reach. These receipts remain independent. The house records its three planes as CRDT sync across explicit peers, local physical custody within named causal islands, and finite public projection through Pronaos/Herm route owners. Node and Browser Lararia remain equal peers with different local substrates; household/regional Herms may carry relay and bounded read faces; Pronaos carries exact arrival bytes; proxy/container layers carry reach and deployment only. Rejected imports: hosted ActivityPub ontology, IPFS pinning as ownership, global DID roster, wall-clock UCAN expiry, Docker DNS as DreamNet identity, proxy-as-Lararium, and CRDT convergence as authority settlement. The next source work remains the contract witness canonical bytes/signer/digest/snapshot contract and the reserved Docker live receipt. Law: borrowed patterns guide a local design when their assumptions are named; they never erase the house's causal, relational, or operator-held boundaries.
