32:Every persisted custody carrier and every act that touches it has exactly one target class. ''D'' dissolves confidential material into rows owned by one PersonaGroup and sealed with that group's face custody key (FCK). ''F'' carries deliberately public material or ciphertext a blind floor may copy; it has no custody decryption key. ''S'' carries a *named* node-only confidential row under a named node principal and opener. A shared verb creates no shared key. A mixed carrier splits before it receives a class. The browser has no vessel custody key (S key). A node has no residual omnibus key: only an actual S row can justify a node custody door. Current `hot`/`cold` mean S-sealed, not target ownership (`vault-carriers.ts:5-22,64-68`). These are operator rulings recorded at `stable-founding-road.mem:205-207`.
